Inkling 2 oracle prompts: the text of each prompt and its token ids, one decimal id a line, no chat template and no BOS (the file's header states
tokenizer.ggml.add_bos_token = false, and `inkling2-oracle.sh --prompts` checks llama-tokenize gives the same ids with and without --no-bos before it
writes a file). A dump of this model's logits takes its ids from here and never tokenizes (tools/ref/cb_dump.cpp): a tokenizer difference would read as
a kernel bug.

Made once, on the box, by the tokenizer of the family's tree (llama.cpp PR #32695, "convert: register the looped Inkling 2 architecture separately",
head 6196d9802e0757a5218f16f91d9a6830793ba800, CPU build, no patch, /home/user/llama.cpp-pr32695) on the Mini's UD-Q4_K_XL GGUF (the pre-tokenizer is
the file's own `inkling2`, the gpt-4o pretokenizer regex; the vocabulary of 200,058 tokens is the unpadded one), by
`bash crates/tokenizer/tools/inkling2-oracle.sh --prompts tools/ref/data/inkling2`:

    llama-tokenize -m <the Mini's GGUF> -f <text> --ids --no-bos --no-escape --log-disable   # "[id, id, ...]", written one id a line

a, b, c and d are the four prompts every model's dump runs (tools/ref/data/hy4, the same bytes: a the English paragraph, b the Korean one, c the Rust
function head, d "The capital of France is"); this tokenizer cuts them wider than Hy4-flash's (35, 35, 39 and 5 ids against 32, 31, 30 and 5).

    a  35 ids   English paragraph, cut after "coming home."      txt 139 bytes
    b  35 ids   Korean paragraph, cut after "단풍이"              txt 97 bytes
    c  39 ids   Rust function head, cut after `HashMap::new();`  txt 115 bytes
    d   5 ids   "The capital of France is"                       txt 24 bytes
    e 1038 ids  the harbor narrative continued to length         txt 4713 bytes

e is the one prompt past the sliding window: the Mini's and the fixture's windowed layers cap at 1,024 keys (attention.sliding_window 1024, and the
local layers' relative-bias extent is the same 1,024), so e's last 14 positions (1024 through 1037) attend exactly 1,024 keys with their oldest rows
dropped, while the four global layers (the visits at slots 5, 11, 17 and 23 and their looped copies) attend the whole prefix. It is also the only
prompt split across ubatches (512 + 512 + 14 at the dumper's -ub 512): the short convolutions' recurrent state and the KV carry across ubatch
boundaries inside one prefill, and every core visit of passes two and three reads a window its own pass filled. a through d (at most 39 ids) never
leave the first ubatch or reach the window.

The tree that dumps the sets is the same commit carrying tools/ref/inkling2-scale.patch — upstream master's own a1f422260 ("model : load ffn_gate_up_exps
scales", #32657), which the PR branch lacks: without it the loader refuses both the Mini's and the fixture's files at the tensor count (their fused NVFP4
stacks' per-expert `ffn_gate_up_exps.scale` rows are never created). The ids above were made before the patch, from the same commit's tokenizer (the patch
touches no tokenizer path); the sets (tools/ref/inkling2-dump.sh, ref_inkling2_{a..e} and the fixture's fx_ twins) come from the patched tree, whose build
line every set names.
